---
description: TIDL compliance, naming, and PHI rules. Non negotiable.
alwaysApply: true
---

- No molecule or drug names on any consumer facing surface. Goal framed, stack
  named language only. Named molecules appear only behind the logged in patient
  portal, inside clinical intake, and on the prescription itself.
- No compoundable molecule appears on any surface until PrescribeRx has
  confirmed its status in writing.
- No celebrity or partner names in any deliverable, internal or external. Use
  partner UGC or celebrity partnership instead.
- No outcome claims. Aspirational copy carries implied outcome risk and needs
  legal and medical review before launch. Conditional statements carry
  "if prescribed".
- Practitioner framed, never vendor framed.
- Write GLP 1 with a space, no dash.
- No PHI in this repo. Ever. PHI stays inside PrescribeRx.
- LegitScript is required only for Google and Meta paid ads, not for the site.
  FDA and FTC promotional rules govern the site regardless.
